event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2845,"item_id":"fc_0ab345649bc6d74b016adb20b721c48191aefe7625c4876bd6","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"For every nonnegative integer n and every nonempty compact E⊆ℝ^n, with I=[0,1] and E×I given the concatenated Euclidean metric, prove dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"nonnegative integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"subset of Euclidean ℝ^n\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-9\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-9\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"case_elimination\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\",\\\"direct\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"natural_induction\\\",\\\"negation_introduction\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Concatenated Euclidean distance has squared value |x−y|²+|t−u|²; projections are 1-Lipschitz, and diam(U×J)≤√(diam(U)²+diam(J)²). Subdivide [0,1] into at most 1/r+1 intervals of length at most r for 0<r≤1.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"ℝ^n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space of dimension n\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The n-dimensional Euclidean space, with ℝ^0 a singleton.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"dim_H\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Hausdorff dimension\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Critical exponent of Hausdorff measures; dim_H(∅)=0.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"I\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"subset of ℝ\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"[0,1].\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"If d<dim_H(A), the d-dimensional Hausdorff measure of A is infinite.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"If d<dim_H(A), the d-dimensional Hausdorff measure of A is infinite.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"A is in an extended metric space with its Borel measurable structure; d is NNReal.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M001-0006/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"55313e0fb359726f773fe001aa619855264b1d97dbf48806a0fe170a60cd1b3b\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH.{u_1} : ∀ {X : Type u_1} [inst : EMetricSpace.{u_1} X] [inst_1 : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} X]\\\\n  [inst_2 :\\\\n    @BorelSpace.{u_1} X\\\\n      (@UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace.{u_1} X\\\\n        (@PseudoEMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.{u_1} X (@EMetricSpace.toPseudoEMetricSpace.{u_1} X inst)))\\\\n      inst_1]\\\\n  {s : Set.{u_1} X} {d : NNReal},\\\\n  @LT.lt.{0} ENNReal (@Preorder.toLT.{0} ENNReal (@PartialOrder.toPreorder.{0} ENNReal ENNReal.instPartialOrder)) (↑d)\\\\n      (@dimH.{u_1} X inst s) →\\\\n    @Eq.{1} ENNReal\\\\n      (@DFunLike.coe.{u_1 + 1, u_1 + 1, 1} (@MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} X inst_1) (Set.{u_1} X) (fun x => ENNReal)\\\\n        (@MeasureTheory.Measure.instFunLike.{u_1} X inst_1)\\\\n        (@MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure.{u_1} X inst inst_1 inst_2 ↑d) s)\\\\n      (@Top.top.{0} ENNReal ENNReal.instTop)\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a countable family of nonnegative measurable ENNReal functions, the integral of the pointwise sum equals the sum of integrals.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a countable family of nonnegative measurable ENNReal functions, the integral of the pointwise sum equals the sum of integrals.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"Measurable space with measure; countable index type; all summands AEMeasurable.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M002-0007/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"01119424cec55e4311d11b42ce3180fd3755062cf5d437e9eb1bef2912cdef85\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue.Add\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"14da3dd3c269221e9ec43e91c6b22bb02d5db7f00e03c789661c72dffecf7b4a\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum.{u_1,\\\\n    u_2} : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {m : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {μ : @MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α m}\\\\n  [Countable.{u_2 + 1} β] {f : β → α → ENNReal},\\\\n  (∀ (i : β), @AEMeasurable.{u_1, 0} α ENNReal ENNReal.measurableSpace m (f i) μ) →\\\\n    @Eq.{1} ENNReal\\\\n      (@MeasureTheory.lintegral.{u_1} α m μ fun a =>\\\\n        @tsum.{0, u_2} ENNReal β ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace (fun i => f i a)\\\\n          (SummationFilter.unconditional.{u_2} β))\\\\n      (@tsum.{0, u_2} ENNReal β ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace\\\\n        (fun i => @MeasureTheory.lintegral.{u_1} α m μ fun a => f i a) (SummationFilter.unconditional.{u_2} β))\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"dim_H\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Set D=dim_H(E), F=E×I. Boundedness from compactness and elementary cube covers of a bounded box show D≤n. For q>D, M001 gives H^q(E)=0. At scale δ≤1 use covers by positive-diameter r_j≤δ with arbitrarily small Σr_j^q; replace singleton members by tiny balls with summable arbitrarily small added cost. Cover I for each j with at most 1/r_j+1 intervals of length ≤r_j. The products cover F, have diameter ≤√2r_j, and total (q+1)-cost ≤2(√2)^(q+1)Σr_j^q. Letting costs and scales tend to zero yields H^(q+1)(F)=0, hence dim_H(F)≤D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"q\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"r_j\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D>0 fix 0<s<D. M001 gives H^s(E)=∞, so scale contents c_s(E,δ) tend to infinity by their defining limit. For an arbitrary cover V_i of F with ρ_i=diam(V_i)≤δ≤1, let A_i,B_i be projections. Enlarge each B_i to an open interval J_i of length ≤ρ_i+η_i, choosing η_i>0 with Ση_iρ_i^s<ε. For every t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E: each (x,t) belongs to some V_i and B_i⊆J_i. Hence c_s(E,δ)≤Σ1_{J_i}(t)ρ_i^s pointwise. These are nonnegative measurable functions; M002 gives integral of the sum equals the sum of integrals. Integrating over I gives c_s(E,δ)≤Σ(ρ_i+η_i)ρ_i^s≤Σρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Zero-diameter terms vanish since s>0. Let ε→0 and infimize over product covers to obtain c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ); hence H^(s+1)(F)=∞ and dim_H(F)≥s+1. Taking every 0<s<D gives dim_H(F)≥D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"s\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"V_i\\\",\\\"ρ_i\\\",\\\"A_i\\\",\\\"B_i\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"η_i\\\",\\\"ε\\\",\\\"c_s\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D=0 choose x₀∈E by H001. The coordinate projection F→I is onto and 1-Lipschitz by the concatenated Euclidean metric. Directly, every countable cover of I has sum of diameters at least 1 (enlarge each covering set to an interval by arbitrarily small errors), so H^1(I)>0 and dim_H(I)≥1. Interval subdivisions show H^q(I)=0 for q>1, giving dim_H(I)≤1. The Lipschitz-cover estimate dim_H(image)≤dim_H(domain) follows by mapping each covering set and using diameter nonincrease. Thus dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. This holds for n=0 too. Combine with upper bound.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"x₀\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply in Euclidean Borel space to E and q>D.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply in Euclidean Borel space to E and 0<s<D.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Use counting measure on I and f_i(t)=ρ_i^s·1_{J_i∩I}(t), measurable since J_i is open.\\\"]}] }]}}\"}"}

